      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Rows: 25 as printed (1926–1949 and 1950–1960). Empty cells are printed as dotted rules, written '...'.",
        "Row checks (5 foreign columns = Total foreign; Remitted + Domestic loans = Total domestic; Total foreign + Total domestic = grand total): all reconcile except: 1926 grand: 89,535 vs printed 89,525; 1927 grand: 90,862 vs printed 90,852; 1928 foreign: parts 39,330 vs printed 39,590; 1929 foreign: parts 39,588 vs printed 39,581; 1930 foreign: parts 39,576 vs printed 39,570; 1931 foreign: parts 39,502 vs printed 39,492; 1932 foreign: parts 33,189 vs printed 33,179; 1933 foreign: parts 24,690 vs printed 24,680; 1933 grand: 62,367 vs printed 62,371; 1934 foreign: parts 24,685 vs printed 24,675; 1935 foreign: parts 24,680 vs printed 24,670; 1936 foreign: parts 24,675 vs printed 24,665; 1937 foreign: parts 24,670 vs printed 24,660; 1938 foreign: parts 24,664 vs printed 24,654; 1939 foreign: parts 24,658 vs printed 24,648; 1940 foreign: parts 24,652 vs printed 24,642; 1941 foreign: parts 22,775 vs printed 22,765; 1942 foreign: parts 22,768 vs printed 22,758; 1943 foreign: parts 22,761 vs printed 22,751; 1944 foreign: parts 15,406 vs printed 15,396; 1945 foreign: parts 15,406 vs printed 15,396",
        "Pattern: in 1929–1945 every printed Total foreign charges is exactly 10 less than the sum of its parts (as if the reorganization loan were 13,454); the 13,464 cells were all re-checked on enlarged crops and read clearly 13,464. 1928: parts with 7,259 give 39,330; printed 39,590 (= 7,529 reading minus 10), so 7,259 looks like a transposition misprint — kept as printed. 1926–1927 foreign totals reconcile but their grand totals are 10 short; 1933 grand total is 4 more than 24,680 + 37,687. All kept as printed.",
        "Row 1928, Russo-French loan: printed 7,259 (other years 7,529); kept as printed.",
        "Row 1941, Remitted portion: a stray mark between '15' and '618'; read 15,618. Row 1941, Domestic loans: dotted rule with a stray mark."
      ],
