      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Rows: 25 as printed (1926-1948, 1949-1960, 1961).",
        "Row 1927, col 'Charges — Domestic': last group blotted (reads '50, 600, 0?0' with an ink spot over the middle digits); written [?].",
        "Row 1938, col 'Charges — Domestic': first digit of the second group partly covered by an ink blot, ambiguous 3 vs 8; the printed balance (Surplus 92,500,000 = 151,000,000 - 24,700,000 - X) fits only 8, so 33,800,000 written (3-vs-8 rule).",
        "'...' = printed dotted rule (nil) in the cell.",
        "Check Net customs revenue = Foreign + Domestic + Surplus: reconciles for 23 of the 24 checkable rows; row 1935 does not (145,000,000 vs 24,700,000 + 37,000,000 + 85,600,000 = 147,300,000; re-read, as printed). Row 1927 not checkable."
      ],
